: Calculate the real roots of a quadratic equation.
: The equation should be in the form:
:   ax^2 + bx + c = 0
: If there is only one real root, it is displayed twice.
: If there are no real roots, and error occurs.

: -01-          a
: -02-          b
: -03-          c

01  ENT         : a, Entering clears the display.
02  MIN
03  M+          : (2a)->M, We store it like this as we only need 2a never a.
04  ENT         : b
05  STO
06   [1]        : b->R1, We need b later.
07  /
08  MR          : (2a)->X
09  =           : v = b / 2a, This is one part of the solution formula.
10  X-S         
11   [1]        : v->R1, b->X, We put the first part aside, and start with b.
12  X^2
13  -
14  MR          : (2a)->X
15  *
16  ENT         : c
17  =           : b^2 - 2ac
18  =           : b^2 - 4ac, The last outer step is repeated.
19  2RX
20  /
21  MR          : (2a)->X
22  =           : w = sqrt(b^2 - 4ac) / 2a, The other part of the formula.
23  MIN         : w->M, We will need this part later.
24  -
25  RCL
26   [1]        : v->X
27  =           : x1 = -v + w, The first root.
28  HLT
29  -
30  MR          : w->X
31  =           : v
32  =           : x2 = -v - w, The second root.
